@startuml cancer-model-en
hide circle
hide empty members
title How a cancer registry record fits together

class Patient [[https://dhp.uz/fhir/core/StructureDefinition-uz-core-patient.html{Open the UZ Core Patient profile}]]
class CancerCondition [[StructureDefinition-cancer-condition.html{Open the CancerCondition profile}]] #E8F0FE
class CancerEpisodeOfCare [[StructureDefinition-cancer-episode-of-care.html{Open the CancerEpisodeOfCare profile}]] #E8F0FE
class CancerEncounter [[StructureDefinition-cancer-encounter.html{Open the CancerEncounter profile}]] #E8F0FE
class CancerObservationTumorMorphology [[StructureDefinition-cancer-observation-tumor-morphology.html{Open the CancerObservationTumorMorphology profile}]] #E8F0FE
class CancerObservationBehavior [[StructureDefinition-cancer-observation-behavior.html{Open the CancerObservationBehavior profile}]] #E8F0FE
class CancerObservationHistologicGrade [[StructureDefinition-cancer-observation-histologic-grade.html{Open the CancerObservationHistologicGrade profile}]] #E8F0FE
class CancerObservationMetastase [[StructureDefinition-cancer-observation-metastase.html{Open the CancerObservationMetastase profile}]] #E8F0FE
class CancerObservationTNMStageGroup [[StructureDefinition-cancer-observation-tnm-stage-group.html{Open the CancerObservationTNMStageGroup profile}]] #E8F0FE
class CancerObservationTNMCategory [[StructureDefinition-cancer-observation-tnm-category.html{Open the CancerObservationTNMCategory profile}]] #E8F0FE


Patient "1" <-- "0..*" CancerEpisodeOfCare : « patient »
Patient "1" <-- "0..*" CancerEncounter : « subject »
Patient "1" <-- "0..*" CancerCondition : « subject »
CancerEpisodeOfCare "0..*" <-- "0..*" CancerEncounter : « episodeOfCare »
CancerEpisodeOfCare "0..*" --> "1" CancerCondition : « diagnosis.condition »
CancerEncounter "0..*" -right-> "1" CancerCondition : « diagnosis.condition »
CancerCondition "0..*" --> "0..1" CancerEncounter : « encounter »
CancerCondition "1" <-- "0..*" CancerObservationTumorMorphology : « focus »
CancerCondition "1" <-- "0..*" CancerObservationMetastase : « focus »
' norank gives this link its own SVG id; two ranked links between the same classes share one
CancerObservationTNMStageGroup "0..*" -[norank]-> "1" CancerCondition : « focus »
CancerCondition "0..*" --> "0..*" CancerObservationTNMStageGroup : « stage.assessment »
CancerObservationTumorMorphology "0..*" --> "0..*" CancerObservationBehavior : « hasMember »
CancerObservationTumorMorphology "0..*" --> "0..*" CancerObservationHistologicGrade : « hasMember »
CancerObservationTNMStageGroup "0..*" --> "0..*" CancerObservationTNMCategory : « hasMember »
CancerCondition "1" <-- "0..*" CancerObservationBehavior : « focus »
CancerCondition "1" <-- "0..*" CancerObservationHistologicGrade : « focus »
CancerCondition "1" <-- "0..*" CancerObservationTNMCategory : « focus »
' keep the observation row in its usual order now that one « focus » link is norank
CancerObservationTumorMorphology -[hidden]right- CancerObservationTNMStageGroup
CancerObservationTNMStageGroup -[hidden]right- CancerObservationMetastase

note "Every Observation also references\nthe Patient through « subject »" as N1
N1 .. CancerObservationMetastase

caption Clinical graph: references to organizations, practitioners and other actors are left out to keep the diagram readable.

@enduml
